Me neither, but I prefer to get MR and reflection before doing that
exhaustive exploration.  If I'm at or below DL8 and have used up the
fountains above me, I'll find a musical instrument and make for the
Castle as quickly as possible to minimize my exposure while I'm
under-equipped.

Once I've gotten the wand and kitted up minimally, I'll go back and
finish exploring the levels above.

The path to ascending a high percentage of games is to ruthlessly
acquire the resistances needed to make the RNG less able to randomly
kill you.  In particular, don't wander around searching aimlessly when
you still lack key resistances and know exactly where to go to acquire
them safely (and with an instrument, the castle is perfectly safe
unless purple L are there--those can often be dealt with safely too as
long as you're careful about checking for them before leaving the
staircase and use the resources you've found wisely).

Getting past possible titans/minotaurs on the way can require care.

But ultimately, making for the Castle after you're pretty tough and
before exhaustively searching is often the _conservative_ strategy
(esp. if you lack MR).



